</code></pre> <p>This writes two files:</p> <ul> <li><code>lib/src/save_blog.g.dart</code>: the checks, the converter and the JSON Schema of <code>SaveBlog</code>.</li> <li><code>lib/dtos.g.dart</code>: the list of every DTO in this package. The server uses it.</li> </ul> <p>Commit both files. Then the Flutter app does not need to run the generator.</p> <p>Rules that need the database stay on the server</p> <p><code>@Unique</code> and <code>@Exists</code> come from <code>dox_orm</code>. Do not use them in the shared package: the app can not import <code>dox_orm</code>. Check them on the server, in the service or in a server-only DTO.</p>

