lib/app/http/controllers/auth.controller.dart<pre><code>import 'package:dox_auth/dox_auth.dart';
import 'package:dox_core/dox_core.dart';
import 'package:my_app/app/models/user/user.model.dart';

@Inject()
class AuthController {
  /// Make an account and log in.
  Future&lt;dynamic&gt; register(RegisterUser body) async {
    User user = User();
    user.name = body.name;
    user.email = body.email;
    user.password = Hash.make(body.password);
    await user.save();

    String? token = Auth().login(user);
    return &lt;String, dynamic&gt;{'token': token, 'user': user};
  }

  /// Check the email and password. Give a token.
  Future&lt;dynamic&gt; login(LoginUser body) async {
    Auth auth = Auth();
    String? token = await auth.attempt(&lt;String, dynamic&gt;{
      'email': body.email,
      'password': body.password,
    });
    if (token == null) {
      throw UnAuthorizedException(message: 'Wrong email or password');
    }
    return &lt;String, dynamic&gt;{'token': token, 'user': auth.user&lt;User&gt;()};
  }

  /// The logged in user.
  User? user(DoxRequest req) {
    return req.auth?.user&lt;User&gt;();
  }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>RegisterUser</code> and <code>LoginUser</code> are <code>@Dto</code> classes. See Validation.</p>

lib/routes/api.dart<pre><code>Route.post&lt;AuthController&gt;('/auth/login', &lt;dynamic&gt;[
  RateLimit(max: 5, per: Duration(minutes: 1)),
  (AuthController c) =&gt; c.login,
]);
</code></pre> <p>Each client (by ip) can now send 5 login requests per minute. The 6th request gets:</p> <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 42
X-RateLimit-Limit: 5
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0

{"code":"too_many_requests","message":"Too Many Requests"}
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>Retry-After</code> is the number of seconds until the client can try again.</li> <li>Every answer, also a normal one, has <code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code> and <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code>.</li> <li>The error goes through your <code>exceptionHandler</code> and <code>responseHandler</code>, like any other error. So it has the same JSON shape as your other errors.</li> </ul> <p>The defaults are <code>max: 60</code> and <code>per: Duration(minutes: 1)</code>.</p>

